# Testability Lite

Make features easy to try and debug — without a full QA framework.

## Frontend

- Add `data-testid` on interactive elements and important status messages
  - Example: `data-testid="health-status"`, `data-testid="submit-button"`
- Prefer semantic names that describe purpose, not styles
- Loading and error states should be visible in the UI (not only in the console)

## Backend

- Return clear error messages and codes (see API contract rule)
- Keep `/health` accurate so local and CI checks can detect a live server
- Log enough context to debug a failure (route, reason) without secrets

## Before you say "done"

- Can someone open the UI and see success vs failure clearly?
- Can someone call the API and understand the JSON without reading the source?
